+## 7. No-release, no-pin, and no-claim guards
+
+Capture external state before any verification work and compare it at handoff:
+
+```bash
+git ls-remote --tags https://github.com/ivanopcode/cocoaskills.git > artifacts/TASK-260720-3s27te/csk-tags.before
+gh release list --repo ivanopcode/cocoaskills --limit 100 --json tagName,isDraft,isPrerelease,publishedAt > artifacts/TASK-260720-3s27te/csk-releases.before.json
+git ls-remote --tags https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec.git > artifacts/TASK-260720-3s27te/spec-tags.before
+gh release list --repo relux-works/curator-spec --limit 100 --json tagName,isDraft,isPrerelease,publishedAt > artifacts/TASK-260720-3s27te/spec-releases.before.json
+```
+
+Repeat into `.after` files, then:
+
+```bash
+cmp artifacts/TASK-260720-3s27te/csk-tags.before artifacts/TASK-260720-3s27te/csk-tags.after
+cmp artifacts/TASK-260720-3s27te/csk-releases.before.json artifacts/TASK-260720-3s27te/csk-releases.after.json
+cmp artifacts/TASK-260720-3s27te/spec-tags.before artifacts/TASK-260720-3s27te/spec-tags.after
+cmp artifacts/TASK-260720-3s27te/spec-releases.before.json artifacts/TASK-260720-3s27te/spec-releases.after.json
+```
+
+Guard repository surfaces and the committed suite pin:
+
+```bash
+git diff --exit-code "$CSK_BASE_SHA"..HEAD -- .github/workflows/release.yml CHANGELOG.md
+```
+
+```bash
+python - <<'PY'
+import re, subprocess
+expected = '0c81c1f8d5321d822be2a2817b05aea03e656e15'
+base = subprocess.check_output(['git', 'show', f'{subprocess.check_output(["git", "merge-base", "HEAD", "origin/main"], text=True).strip()}:.github/workflows/ci.yml'], text=True)
+head = subprocess.check_output(['git', 'show', 'HEAD:.github/workflows/ci.yml'], text=True)
+pattern = re.compile(r'ref:\s*([0-9a-f]{40})')
+assert expected in pattern.findall(base)
+assert expected in pattern.findall(head)
+PY
+```
+
+```bash
+git diff --unified=0 "$CSK_BASE_SHA"..HEAD -- . | rg -n '^\+.*(claims_emitted|conformance.claim|v1\.0\.0-rc\.6|softprops/action-gh-release|git tag|gh release)'
+```
+
+The last command is an **expected-red diagnostic** when no suspicious additions exist: its correct result is exit 1 with no matches, and it must be recorded as a non-zero expected absence check, not a passing green gate. Any match requires manual disposition and is a stop until proven harmless. The four `cmp` commands are the authoritative green external-state gates.
